---
// The client's brand fonts, rendered into <head> (dashboard #1485; the body role added in #1521).
//
// Astro's <Font> emits the @font-face rules for the downloaded files, the `:root { --font-primary:
// … }` declaration core's `font-brand` shortcut reads, and the preload links. It is also the one
// piece of this feature that can THROW: given a cssVariable no family registered, it raises
// FontFamilyNotFound and fails the build. That is exactly the state a site is in before its client
// picks a font — i.e. the common case — so each render is gated.
//
// `fontData` from astro:assets is the gate, and it is the RIGHT gate: it is built from the same
// `config.fonts` array cmsFonts() writes, so it answers "did the config side register this?" with
// the config side's own answer, rather than re-deriving it from the API and risking the two
// disagreeing (branding fetched twice, one call failing). A family Astro registered but could not
// resolve — Google unreachable — is present here with an empty array, which is the intended
// outcome: <Font> then emits the variable carrying only the fallback stack, and the page renders
// in system type instead of failing.
//
// The two roles are gated separately because they are separate choices: a client may set a display
// face and no body face, or the reverse, and the build may have dropped one of the two at its
// preflight while keeping the other.
//
// `--font-body` is a token this PUBLISHES, not one core applies. Running text inherits from
// `body`, whose rule lives in the site's own global.css — unlayered, and therefore unbeatable by
// anything core could write. A site adopts the body face with one line there:
//
//   body { font-family: var(--font-body, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif); }
//
// Sites render this once, in the layout head:
//
//   import BrandFont from '@rocksoft/cms-starter-core/core/BrandFont.astro'
//   <BrandFont />
import { Font, fontData } from 'astro:assets'
import { FONT_ROLES } from './fonts.mjs'

interface Props {
  /** Emit preload links for the font files. Off by default — see below. */
  preload?: boolean
}

const { preload = false } = Astro.props

// `Object.hasOwn`, not a truthiness check: a registered-but-unresolved family is `[]`, which is
// falsy and is precisely the case that must still render (fallback stack, no failed build).
const registered = FONT_ROLES.map(({ cssVariable }) => cssVariable).filter((cssVariable) =>
  Object.hasOwn(fontData, cssVariable),
)
---

{/*
  Preload is opt-in rather than on: the brand faces style headings and body copy, so preloading
  them competes with the LCP image on most of these pages. A site whose hero is typographic passes
  `preload`.
*/}
{registered.map((cssVariable) => <Font cssVariable={cssVariable} preload={preload} />)}
